Description: join an Ubuntu desktop to Microsoft Entra ID with Himmelblau
 Sesame joins an Ubuntu Desktop 24.04 or newer to Microsoft Entra ID the way
 a Windows PC does, through Himmelblau: no Entra application or tenant ID to
 create. You give your work address and a machine name; your existing local
 account is linked to your Entra account and keeps its UID, home directory
 and settings. You sign in with the Entra password and confirm on your
 phone.
 .
 Every step detects whether it is already done and can be run again. The
 configuration is backed up first, and a rescue administrator account is
 created. Himmelblau (stable branch) is built on the machine, as the user
 and without root, then installed; this takes about 30 to 60 minutes and is
 queued by Gagarine when it is present.
 .
 It comes as a graphical assistant ("sesame-assistant", GTK 4 and
 libadwaita, which needs the recommended packages), a command line
 ("sesame") and a root helper launched through pkexec.
 .
 The package installs a signed APT repository entry, so "apt upgrade" keeps
 Sesame up to date.

